      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>This Aramaic poem, written in the early Byzantine era by an unknown author, can be found in its entirety within the Targum Sheni for Esther 7:9. It features an argument between an assortment of trees over which one is required to bear the great dishonor of having to be the one to hold Haman. It’s also chock-full of anti-Christian polemic and references to Sefer Toldot Yeshu. The translation preserves the somewhat ragged acrostic. Two lines [in brackets] were invented by the author to fill lacunae in the verses.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_54642_introduction"/>
